+
+### Conventional digital VFO modes
+
+The VFO mode value also accepts P25 (2) and NXDN (3) when built in. In these modes, the saved RX and TX tone values
+hold the receive and transmit NAC/RAN, and the saved talk target holds the 16-bit talkgroup. Tone types are NONE.
+The settings record size and version are unchanged; existing FM/DMR records retain their interpretation.
+Both VFOs use this representation. An older build without these modes falls back to its default VFO mode.
