+
+### Conventional digital VFO operation
+
+The mode request accepts P25 and NXDN in a VFO when built in, alongside FM and DMR. The quick-settings Mode tile
+cycles those four modes and skips unsupported ones. Trunking is excluded. Entering P25 selects NAC 0x293 and TG 1;
+entering NXDN selects RAN 1 and TG 1. Both use the existing digital channel RX/TX paths and their safety checks.
+Copy to VFO preserves a conventional digital channel's NAC/RAN and group; saving and restoring both VFOs uses the
+mode-dependent representation in [Settings store](settings-store.md#conventional-digital-vfo-modes).
